ich by the way  the country has committed itself  as a founding member of the council of  europe  i am deeply worried about the fact that  turkey withdrew from the istanbul  convention  this is about protecting women and  protecting  children against violence and this is  clearly the wrong signal  right now the european union will never  hesitate  to point out further negative  developments  and this is also true for unilateral  actions  against eu member states like greece or  cyprus  in some we want to move forward towards  much better relations in future  but we are at the beginning of this road  and the weeks and months ahead will  show how far we can go on this road  together  thank you  thank you miss and mr president and we  are going to take  three questions if you are loved each  sort of jazz  from the reuters news agency uh i had a  question about the timetable of the  planned steps that you mentioned just  now uh it seems that ankara wants these  steps to be implemented rather  quickly whereas the eu is proposing this  as more of a process that might take  some time  during your meeting with president  erdogan today did you have a chance to  discuss a concrete timeline for these  steps  and secondly what impression did you get  from president erdogan about remaining  true to the commitments that turkey has  made in terms of de-escalation  thank you very much this was in my  opinion an important uh  meeting an important moment because  because it was the opportunity for us to  to explain  what's the european vision and what's a  possible positive agenda  based on what we think should be the  priorities in the  in the future but there is one certainty  uh  i intend to put again this point at the  agenda on the gender of the open council  in june  uh it means that now the commission  will work very actively and probably  also in partnership  with the turkish authorities in order to  prepare  to prepare the next steps  yes indeed so  this is the beginning of 